      "document_classification": "HUMAN_ONLY",
      "inputText": "Psychology is the science that studies the mind and behavior in interaction with context. Although these concepts may sound familiar, they are notably difficult to define. Philosophers and scientists have tried for hundreds of years to delimit the entities we refer to when we use them, without reaching a definitive agreement. For that reason, one of the most obvious and natural questions when we become interested in this science is also one of the most difficult to answer: “What does psychology study?” In this learning project we will try to answer that question. We will not do so by proposing a definition, but by taking a high-level tour through this field of study. In this way we hope to give a general idea of its scope and to familiarize the reader with the basic concepts needed to go deeper into other topics of interest related to the “human mind.”\n\nGeneral objective\n\nSpecific objectives\n\nLessons\n\nBlock 1\n\nLesson 1\n\nIn this lesson we will study the main psychological schools, also known as the great classical theories of psychology.\n\nLesson 2\n\nIn this lesson we will study the main areas into which both the study of psychology (basic psychology) and its application to solving practical problems (applied psychology) are divided.\n\nLesson 3\n\nThis lesson will focus on the practice of psychology, both in the field of research and in the area of professional application.\n\nPartial Evaluation\n\nBlock 2\n\nLesson 4\n\nIn this lesson we will take a brief look at the structure of neurons and how they function.\n\nLesson 5\n\nIn this lesson we will explore the different parts of the human brain and their main functions.\n\nLesson 6\n\nIn this lesson we will explore the techniques available for studying the functioning of the human brain.\n\nPartial Evaluation\n\nBlock 3\n\nLesson 7\n\nIn this lesson we will study consciousness and its different states.\n\nLesson 8\n\nIn this lesson we will explore the concepts of sensation, perception, attention, motivation, emotion, and memory.\n\nLesson 9\n\nLanguage, thought, intelligence, and learning are the cognitive processes we will learn about in this lesson.\n\nPartial Evaluation\n\nBlock 4\n\nLesson 10\n\nThe changes human beings face as they move through the different stages of life will be the area of interest of this lesson.\n\nLesson 11\n\nIn this lesson we will explore the scope and topics of interest of social psychology.\n\nLesson 12\n\nThe concept of abnormality, the types of mental disorders, and the options for their treatment will be the topics of this lesson.\n\nPartial Evaluation\n\nFinal Evaluation\n\nActivities\n\nProposed activity: Glossary of psychological terms\n\nDescription: Review the readings in this learning project by compiling a list of the most important psychological terms and a short definition for each of them.\n\nAdditional material\n\nRelated learning projects\n\nResources in other Wikimedia projects\n\nExternal resources\n\nCategory: Psychology\n\nCategory: University Education Level\n\nCategory: Learning projects\n",
